    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
## What it does

Trains a Kraken model to locate text baselines and regions on page images using
`ketos segtrain`. Train from scratch, fine-tune existing segmentation weights,
or resume a training checkpoint.

## Inputs

Provide page images paired with PAGE XML or ALTO annotations containing baseline
coordinates and region polygons. Text transcriptions are not required. Select
pairs individually or use a `list:paired` collection: the forward element is the
image and the reverse element is its annotation. The tool updates XML image
references for the job. Split multi-page TIFF files into individual pages first.

Validation can use a fraction of the input pages or separate image/annotation
pairs. A split needs enough whole pages to leave at least one training page and
one validation page. Explicit validation is useful for small datasets. Keep
validation pages separate from training pages when assessing model quality.

## Class mappings

Labels are assigned automatically by default. Select **Set class labels explicitly**
to configure `line_class_mapping` and `region_class_mapping`. Enter annotation
class names and integer output labels starting at 2 (0 and 1 are reserved).
For example, map baseline type `default` to 2 and region type `text` to 3.
Baseline and region labels must not overlap. Within one category, assigning the
same label to multiple types merges them; the first type is the exported name.
Use `*` for a fallback label for unlisted types. Without a fallback, unlisted
types are ignored. Leave one category empty to disable training for it; provide
at least one mapping in the other category.

These settings apply to new training and fresh runs from existing models.
Resuming restores the checkpoint's saved mappings. For fresh runs with changed
classes, select the appropriate output class resizing option.

## Training and outputs

The outputs are the best model weights, a text training report, training
checkpoints, and TensorBoard logs. Exported weights can be used for Kraken
segmentation. Checkpoints retain optimizer and training-loop state.

Loading weights or a checkpoint starts a fresh run. Class resizing controls
whether new baseline/region classes can be added or replace the old classes.
Resuming restores the checkpoint's saved data configuration: supply the same
images and annotations in their original order, with the same input format and
validation setup. Checkpoints with paths from another tool or machine may need
their original files and cannot necessarily be resumed here. When resuming,
set epochs to the total desired epoch count, including already completed epochs.
Upload checkpoints as binary data so Galaxy preserves the container intact.

Kraken is licensed under the Apache-2.0 license.
    ]]></help>
